description: Do not execute user-provided tests/commands until the user says run
alwaysApply: true
---

# Wait for explicit run

Do not run anything the user provides (tests, commands, scripts, Playwright, npm, shell, browser). Prepare and write only.

Execute **only** after they say **run**, **run it**, **execute**, or **go ahead and run**.

“Try”, “check”, “verify”, “test this”, or “see if it works” is not permission to run.

This overrides other skills that want to execute (verification, TDD watch-it-fail) until the user says run.

**REQUIRED:** Follow `wait-for-explicit-run` skill.
